  "interpretive_limits": [
    "Importance is conditional on the six declared future inputs and saved entering states; changing a parameter does not reconstruct its pre-anchor history.",
    "Metrics describe open-loop point trajectories; there are no noisy observations, voltage corrections, re-estimation, posterior propagation or prediction-coverage qualification.",
    "Actual propagated SOC depends only on entering SOC and Q in this model. Voltage sensitivity of other coordinates is not their effect on an operating estimator SOC.",
    "OCV-equivalent SOC is 100 deltaV/Uprime with other voltage terms fixed; it is a proxy, not actual SOC error or a bound.",
    "Peak values are from the 35 Hz grid including t0; later current-switch instantaneous limits are absent. Plateau peak indices can depend on floating-point tie-breaking.",
    "RMS excludes t0 and uses every equal-duration sample. Compact nonuniform plot profiles cannot independently reproduce those RMS values.",
    "Exact isolated effects, conditional repairs and joint error are different decompositions. Signed effects can cancel; their absolute sum and RMS ratio are diagnostics, not certified bounds or a bounded cancellation fraction.",
    "One-percent physical-parameter differential units differ from absolute entering-state units. Neither normalized sensitivity nor maximum-over-protocol ranking is universal importance.",
    "Selected C points independently validate stored values; exhaustive nonlinear peak searches were not rerun. The full-grid metric code was reviewed."
